{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Sch_{fppf}/S$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0009": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0010": "$U/S$", "MATH_0011": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0013": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-section-localize}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-big-small-fppf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:303ed10af359e4e22041ab6a07f9a09b0b58678dbe8ad93db077796cc9a5bbba", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:69610f7e023522efee148f6f1191580ae0f8ac8c49113373eecd0d9a66796811", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a big fppf\nsite containing <MATH_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The <TEXTITOPEN_0001>big fppf site of <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, denoted\n<MATH_0005>, is the site <MATH_0006>\nintroduced in Sites, Section <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0003> The <TEXTITOPEN_0002>big affine fppf site of <MATH_0007><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>, denoted\n<MATH_0008>, is the full subcategory of\n<MATH_0009> whose objects are affine <MATH_0010>.\nA covering of <MATH_0011> is any covering\n<MATH_0012> of <MATH_0013> which is a\nstandard fppf covering.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e59caeadffb44e5fb674f79d2a6473e715b744605519b592cc03af73bb815b44", "unit_id": "tag:021S:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6945887321fe30912185bfe21c93363c5ca2e2a223ff071a1d0afa8ad2cf0e45", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt is not completely clear that\nthe big affine fppf site is a site. We check this now.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:65c18f66cd088c5db8cf25ce555abfecf443d46de5c5188cd96a90405353f70e", "unit_id": "tag:021L:prose-0005"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{fppf}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-verify-site-fppf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3b083bddc55008428e0b44554b9cee53e584dc2bd432dde6889f1d99c1436591", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b429c5159e96ad8a86df05b6a8cd8432769b86539d00001b6f9bd0a86b76b9d4", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a big fppf\nsite containing <MATH_0003>. Then <MATH_0004> is a site.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:76b5811c41714eacb8838af976d114ce64574c22cdade9cf8b85dfc66ae8fa1b", "unit_id": "tag:021T:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$i$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T_i\\}_{j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T\\}_{i \\in I, j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\bigcup_{i\\in I} J_i$", "MATH_0007": "$T_{ij}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-verify-site-etale}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-definition-site}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d253dcb1f56998eeee55ef0cda90a7b4563ef30eccfcf8098b1f6f35871bd7ac", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8713bb4719ca5f6bdf39a77c2b05e122ad1387e8d235a15a12017d75c9db05bd", "source_text": "Let us show that <MATH_0001> is a site.\nReasoning as in the proof of Lemma <REF_0001>\nit suffices to show that the collection\nof standard fppf coverings of affines satisfies properties\n(1), (2) and (3) of\nSites, Definition <REF_0002>.\nThis is clear since for example, given a standard fppf\ncovering <MATH_0002> and for each\n<MATH_0003> we have a standard fppf covering <MATH_0004>, then\n<MATH_0005> is a standard fppf covering\nbecause <MATH_0006> is finite and each <MATH_0007> is affine.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4b0424c83cf480ab8ab6d6367b6f71f5f7b7fd26f58f7adcc14d33e5f7d3855d", "unit_id": "tag:021T:proof"}
